    "result_text": "The full test suite is green.\n\nI implemented the `initials` feature with two changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (`\"J.S.\"` for \"john smith\").\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response flows through `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the new field appears automatically. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` for `AcceptanceTest`, and the overall build reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
